-- החלטת ועדת המעקב העליונה (19.2.2015) — פרקי זמן השהייה לקידום בדרגות
-- ומכסת 1,800 המשרות: the supreme follow-up committee, under §160 of the
-- base agreement of 25.12.2008, lengthens every waiting period of §38(ב)
-- and (ו) by one month from 1.3.2015, and the longest hold-back of §38(ט)
-- with them; carries the decision of 19.9.2010 over to a teacher leaving on
-- 31 August whom the longer period would have caught; and, notwithstanding
-- the quotas of §38(ז), approves once 1,800 positions of promotion to
-- grades 7–9 in תשע"ד and תשע"ה, filled in three rounds (1.9.2014,
-- 1.8.2015, 1.9.2015) by the conditions of §ח.
--
-- It amends §38, so it imports it (`base-agreement-38`) and writes each
-- replaced subsection as the new rule, dated; it applies the decision of
-- 19.9.2010, so it imports that decision's module; and it is taken under
-- §160 (`base-agreement-160`). The Ministry's letter of 25.12.2008 (the
-- professional-development hours) is in the corpus with the base
-- agreement's signed copy, and encoded there; the evaluation measures of
-- תשע"ב and תשע"ה are not in the corpus. What they decide is an input here.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `2010-09-19_ofek-hadash_vaadat-maakav_darga-promotion-at-service-end`

§ `החלטת ועדת המעקב העליונה — פרקי זמן השהייה ומכסת 1,800 המשרות — 19.2.2015`

-- akn:preamble The decision's frame: a label row with no text of its own.

-- The day of the decision, written in by hand.
@ref akn:preamble/p1
`the day of the 2015 stay-periods decision` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 19 2 2015

-- akn:preamble/p2 The registration stamp under the Collective Agreements Law (21.06.2015, no. 74/2015); no rule.

-- The opening: the committee, by its power under §160 of the base agreement
-- ("הסכם אופק חדש"), decides on promotion in grades of Ofek Hadash
-- teachers, §38(ז) included, teachers having been placed in grades 7 and 8
-- up to תשע"ד beyond its rates. The three who sign are the three §160 seats
-- on the committee: the wages commissioner at the Treasury, the union's
-- secretary-general and the Ministry's director-general.
@ref akn:preamble/p3 akn:conclusions/t1 akn:conclusions/p2
`the 2015 decision's signatories` MEANS
    LIST `the wages commissioner at the Treasury`, `the teachers' union`, `the Ministry of Education`

#ASSERT all (GIVEN p YIELD elem p `the supreme committee's members`) `the 2015 decision's signatories`
#ASSERT count `the 2015 decision's signatories` EQUALS count `the supreme committee's members`

-- The day §§א–ג take effect.
`1 March 2015` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2015

§§ `א. פרקי זמן השהייה לקידום לדרגות 2 עד 6 (במקום סעיף 38(ב))`

-- From 1.3.2015 §38(ב) reads: from grade 1 to 2 and from 2 to 3, two years
-- and a month in the grade below; from 3 to 4, 4 to 5 and 5 to 6, three
-- years and a month. Written in months: 25 and 37.
@ref akn:art_a
GIVEN `to grade` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `months in the grade below for promotion to grades 2–6 from 1.3.2015` `to grade` IS
    BRANCH IF `to grade` AT MOST 3 THEN 25
           OTHERWISE 37

§§ `ב. פרקי זמן השהייה לקידום לדרגות 7 עד 9 (במקום סעיף 38(ו))`

-- From 1.3.2015 §38(ו) reads: from 6 to 7, 7 to 8 and 8 to 9, three years
-- and a month in the grade below.
@ref akn:art_b
GIVEN `to grade` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `months in the grade below for promotion to grades 7–9 from 1.3.2015` `to grade` IS
    37

-- §38(ב) and (ו) as the base agreement wrote them, in months.
GIVEN `to grade` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `months in the grade below §38 asked before 1.3.2015` `to grade` IS
    12 TIMES `years in the grade below for promotion to` `to grade`

-- The two replaced subsections together: the months the grade below asks
-- for a promotion due on a day. §ה: the day is the one the promotion would
-- have fallen due on under the periods before this decision; from 1.3.2015
-- (convention dates.start: the day itself is in) the new periods govern.
@ref akn:art_a akn:art_b
GIVEN `to grade` IS A NUMBER, `due on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `months in the grade below for promotion to` `to grade` `due on` IS
    IF `due on` `is on or after` `1 March 2015`
    THEN IF `to grade` AT MOST 6
         THEN `months in the grade below for promotion to grades 2–6 from 1.3.2015` `to grade`
         ELSE `months in the grade below for promotion to grades 7–9 from 1.3.2015` `to grade`
    ELSE `months in the grade below §38 asked before 1.3.2015` `to grade`

-- Every period is the base agreement's plus one month: 24 + 1, 36 + 1.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN g YIELD `months in the grade below for promotion to` g `1 March 2015` EQUALS `months in the grade below §38 asked before 1.3.2015` g PLUS 1) (range 2 9)
#ASSERT `months in the grade below for promotion to` 2 (DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2015) EQUALS 24
#ASSERT `months in the grade below for promotion to` 7 `1 March 2015` EQUALS 37
-- From grade 1 to grade 9: 13 + 9 years and eight months.
#ASSERT sum (map (GIVEN g YIELD `months in the grade below for promotion to` g `1 March 2015`) (range 2 9)) EQUALS 22 TIMES 12 PLUS 8

§§ `ג. העיכוב המרבי בקידום לדרגות 7 עד 9 (במקום סעיף 38(ט))`

-- From 1.3.2015 §38(ט) reads: notwithstanding (ח), a teacher who met the
-- conditions of (ה) for grades 7–9 is not held back from them longer than
-- three years and a month (grade 7), four years and a month (grade 8) or
-- five years and a month (grade 9), subject to a free place in the quota.
@ref akn:art_c
GIVEN `to grade` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `months a qualified teacher may be held back from, from 1.3.2015` `to grade` IS
    BRANCH IF `to grade` EQUALS 7 THEN 37
           IF `to grade` EQUALS 8 THEN 49
           OTHERWISE 61

GIVEN `to grade` IS A NUMBER, `due on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `months a qualified teacher may be held back from` `to grade` `due on` IS
    IF `due on` `is on or after` `1 March 2015`
    THEN `months a qualified teacher may be held back from, from 1.3.2015` `to grade`
    ELSE 12 TIMES `years a qualified teacher may be held back from` `to grade`

-- Once held back that long, the next free place is his, before the scores
-- of (ח) — as the base agreement's (ט), in months. The months held back are
-- counted from the day he met the conditions of (ה) (the reading of
-- F-ofek-hadash-2016-stay-periods-a, which the agreement of 31.8.2016
-- brings to light).
GIVEN `to grade` IS A NUMBER, `months held back` IS A NUMBER, `free places` IS A NUMBER, `due on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `goes before the scores under the 2015 hold-back` `to grade` `months held back` `free places` `due on` IF
        `months held back` AT LEAST `months a qualified teacher may be held back from` `to grade` `due on`
    AND `free places` GREATER THAN 0

#ASSERT all (GIVEN g YIELD `months a qualified teacher may be held back from` g `1 March 2015` EQUALS 12 TIMES `years a qualified teacher may be held back from` g PLUS 1) (LIST 7, 8, 9)
#ASSERT NOT `goes before the scores under the 2015 hold-back` 7 36 1 `1 March 2015`
#ASSERT `goes before the scores under the 2015 hold-back` 7 36 1 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2015)

§§ `ד. מי שמסיים את העסקתו — החלת החלטת 2010`

-- A teacher who meets §1(א), (ב) and (ד) of the decision of 19.9.2010
-- ("החלטת 2010": on Ofek Hadash terms, leaving the civil service on 31
-- August, every other condition met on the 31 July before), and in whom
-- §1(ג) (the waiting period ends on the day he leaves) would have held but
-- for this decision's longer periods, is promoted as if the waiting period
-- had ended on that 31 July; §2 of that decision (from the 1 August before)
-- applies to him. Written as the 2010 decision read on the leaver with his
-- waiting period taken to end on the day he leaves.
@ref akn:art_d
GIVEN e IS AN `employee at the end of service`
      `the period would have ended on the day he leaves but for this decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `employee at the end of service`
DECIDE `the leaver as §ד of the 2015 decision reads him` e `the period would have ended on the day he leaves but for this decision` IS
    `employee at the end of service` WITH
        `employed on Ofek Hadash terms`             IS e's `employed on Ofek Hadash terms`
        `ends employment in the civil service on`   IS e's `ends employment in the civil service on`
        `the waiting period for the next grade ends on` IS
            IF `the period would have ended on the day he leaves but for this decision`
            THEN e's `ends employment in the civil service on`
            ELSE e's `the waiting period for the next grade ends on`
        `met the other conditions for promotion on 31 July before the end` IS e's `met the other conditions for promotion on 31 July before the end`

GIVEN e IS AN `employee at the end of service`, `but for this decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `promoted under §ד of the 2015 decision` e `but for this decision` IF
    `the decision applies to` (`the leaver as §ד of the 2015 decision reads him` e `but for this decision`)

GIVEN e IS AN `employee at the end of service`, `but for this decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `the §ד promotion starts on` e `but for this decision` IS
    `the promotion of §1 starts on` (`the leaver as §ד of the 2015 decision reads him` e `but for this decision`)

-- A teacher leaving on 31.8.2015 whose two years for grade 2 would have
-- ended that day; the extra month moves them to 30.9.2015. §ד promotes him
-- from 1.8.2015, as the 2010 decision would have.
`a teacher leaving on 31.8.2015, a month short` MEANS
    `employee at the end of service` WITH
        `employed on Ofek Hadash terms`             IS TRUE
        `ends employment in the civil service on`   IS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2015
        `the waiting period for the next grade ends on` IS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 9 2015
        `met the other conditions for promotion on 31 July before the end` IS TRUE

#ASSERT NOT `the decision applies to` `a teacher leaving on 31.8.2015, a month short`
#ASSERT `promoted under §ד of the 2015 decision` `a teacher leaving on 31.8.2015, a month short` TRUE
#ASSERT `the §ד promotion starts on` `a teacher leaving on 31.8.2015, a month short` TRUE EQUALS JUST (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2015)
#ASSERT NOT `promoted under §ד of the 2015 decision` `a teacher leaving on 31.8.2015, a month short` FALSE

§§ `ה. תחולה על מי שהיה זכאי לקידום מיום 1.3.2015`

-- §§א–ג apply also to a teacher who, but for this decision, would have
-- been entitled to a promotion from 1.3.2015 on: the day that decides
-- which periods govern is the day the promotion would have fallen due
-- under the periods before (`months in the grade below for promotion to`
-- and `months a qualified teacher may be held back from` take that day).
@ref akn:art_e
GIVEN `would have been due on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2015 periods govern a promotion that would have been due on` `would have been due on` IF
    `would have been due on` `is on or after` `1 March 2015`

#ASSERT `the 2015 periods govern a promotion that would have been due on` `1 March 2015`
#ASSERT NOT `the 2015 periods govern a promotion that would have been due on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2015)

§§ `ו. מכסת 1,800 המשרות`

-- Notwithstanding §38(ז), the promotion of teachers to grades 7–9 in the
-- school years תשע"ד and תשע"ה (opening 1.9.2013 and 1.9.2014) is approved
-- once, up to 1,800 positions ("מכסת המשרות").
@ref akn:art_f
`the 1,800 positions` MEANS 1800

`the school years of the 1,800 positions` MEANS LIST DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2013, DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2014

`the 1,800 positions are approved once` MEANS TRUE

-- F-ofek-hadash-2015-stay-periods-a: §ו sets §38(ז) aside ("על אף האמור
-- בסעיף 38(ז)"), and §ט says §§א–ו take nothing from §38(ז) — nor from
-- (ח), which §ג's new (ט) is "notwithstanding". The reading adopted
-- (convention precedence.specific): §ו and §ג govern the matter each
-- names; §ט keeps the rest of those subsections.
`the subsections §ו sets aside` MEANS LIST "38(ז)"
`the subsections §ג sets aside` MEANS LIST "38(ח)"

§§ `ז. מה אינו נמנה במכסה`

-- The teachers placed in grades 7–9 on the day of signing, and the
-- positions free for promotion to grade 9 on that day, are not in the
-- 1,800: a promotion to grade 9 into a position free at the signing takes
-- nothing from it.
@ref akn:art_g
`the positions held in grades 7–9 at the signing count in the 1,800` MEANS FALSE

@desc A teacher in the rounds of §ח.
DECLARE `candidate for the 1,800 positions` HAS
    `the candidate's number`  IS A NUMBER @desc any number that tells candidates apart
    `seeks grade`             IS A NUMBER @desc 7, 8 or 9
    `position share`          IS A NUMBER @desc the share of a position he is promoted in
    `fills a grade-9 position free at the signing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `finished the professional-development hours on` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc the hours the grade asks by the Ministry's letter to the union of 25.12.2008, which the corpus does not hold
    `months counted in the grade below by 1.9.2014`  IS A NUMBER @desc counted as §38(ג)–(ד) count them
    `months counted in the grade below by 1.8.2015`  IS A NUMBER
    `months counted in the grade below by 31.8.2015` IS A NUMBER
    `evaluated sufficient by the תשע"ב measures`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc the evaluation measures set for תשע"ב, which the corpus does not hold
    `the תשע"ב evaluation score`                      IS A NUMBER
    `retires on 31.8.2015`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the תשע"ה evaluation score`                      IS A NUMBER

GIVEN c IS A `candidate for the 1,800 positions`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the positions a promotion takes from the 1,800` c IS
    IF c's `seeks grade` EQUALS 9 AND c's `fills a grade-9 position free at the signing`
    THEN 0
    ELSE c's `position share`

§§ `ח. שלושת הסבבים`

-- akn:art_h The opening of §ח: the promotion within the 1,800 only, by (1)–(3).

GIVEN c IS A `candidate for the 1,800 positions`, `by` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `finished the professional-development hours by` c `by` IF
    CONSIDER c's `finished the professional-development hours on`
    WHEN JUST d THEN d `is on or before` `by`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

GIVEN c IS A `candidate for the 1,800 positions`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `seeks grade 7, 8 or 9` c IF
    c's `seeks grade` AT LEAST 7 AND c's `seeks grade` AT MOST 9

-- (1): promoted to grade 7, 8 or 9 with effect from 1.9.2014 who (א)
-- finished the grade's professional-development hours by 1.9.2014, (ב)
-- completed the waiting period of §38(ו) by 1.9.2014 — §38(ו) as it read
-- that day, before §ב's month (convention instruments.governing-term: the
-- rule that governs the matter on the day it is applied) — and (ג) was
-- evaluated sufficient by the measures set for תשע"ב.
@ref akn:art_h__para_1 akn:art_h__para_1__subpara_a akn:art_h__para_1__subpara_b akn:art_h__para_1__subpara_c
`1 September 2014` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2014

GIVEN c IS A `candidate for the 1,800 positions`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the first round of §ח` c IF
        `seeks grade 7, 8 or 9` c
    AND `finished the professional-development hours by` c `1 September 2014`
    AND c's `months counted in the grade below by 1.9.2014` AT LEAST `months in the grade below for promotion to` (c's `seeks grade`) `1 September 2014`
    AND c's `evaluated sufficient by the תשע"ב measures`

`the first round's promotions take effect` MEANS `1 September 2014`

-- (2): where places are left after (1), promoted to grade 7, 8 or 9 on
-- 1.8.2015 who (א) finished the hours by 1.8.2015, (ב) completed by
-- 1.8.2015 the waiting period of §38(ו) — as §ב reads it that day — "for
-- promotion to grade 7 or grade 8", (ג) was evaluated sufficient by the
-- תשע"ב measures and (ד) retires on 31.8.2015.
-- F-ofek-hadash-2015-stay-periods-b: (ב) names grades 7 and 8 only, where
-- the opening of (2) and its (א) promote to grade 9 too. The reading
-- adopted (convention reading.misprint): the waiting period is the one for
-- the grade sought, 9 included.
@ref akn:art_h__para_2 akn:art_h__para_2__subpara_a akn:art_h__para_2__subpara_b akn:art_h__para_2__subpara_c akn:art_h__para_2__subpara_d
`1 August 2015` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2015

GIVEN c IS A `candidate for the 1,800 positions`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the second round of §ח` c IF
        `seeks grade 7, 8 or 9` c
    AND `finished the professional-development hours by` c `1 August 2015`
    AND c's `months counted in the grade below by 1.8.2015` AT LEAST `months in the grade below for promotion to` (c's `seeks grade`) `1 August 2015`
    AND c's `evaluated sufficient by the תשע"ב measures`
    AND c's `retires on 31.8.2015`

`the second round's promotions take effect` MEANS `1 August 2015`

-- (3): where places are left after (1) and (2), promoted to grade 7, 8 or
-- 9 on 1.9.2015 who (א) finished the hours by 31.8.2015 and (ב) completed
-- the waiting period of §38(ו) "for promotion to grade 7 or grade 8" by
-- 31.8.2015 (the same reading as (2)(ב)), and (ג) had the highest תשע"ה
-- evaluation results among those who meet (א) and (ב).
@ref akn:art_h__para_3 akn:art_h__para_3__subpara_a akn:art_h__para_3__subpara_b akn:art_h__para_3__subpara_c
`31 August 2015` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2015

GIVEN c IS A `candidate for the 1,800 positions`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the third round's (א) and (ב)` c IF
        `seeks grade 7, 8 or 9` c
    AND `finished the professional-development hours by` c `31 August 2015`
    AND c's `months counted in the grade below by 31.8.2015` AT LEAST `months in the grade below for promotion to` (c's `seeks grade`) `31 August 2015`

`the third round's promotions take effect` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2015

-- The grades the later rounds promote to, and the grades their (ב) names.
`the grades §ח(2) and §ח(3) promote to` MEANS LIST 7, 8, 9
`the grades §ח(2)(ב) and §ח(3)(ב) name` MEANS LIST 7, 8

`the later rounds' waiting period names no grade 9` MEANS
        elem 9 `the grades §ח(2) and §ח(3) promote to`
    AND NOT elem 9 `the grades §ח(2)(ב) and §ח(3)(ב) name`
#ASSERT `the later rounds' waiting period names no grade 9`

-- Who a round's places reach. (3) ranks by the תשע"ה results; (1) and (2)
-- promote every teacher who meets them and say nothing of more teachers
-- than places. F-ofek-hadash-2015-stay-periods-c: the reading adopted is
-- §38(ח)'s order, which §ט keeps — the highest evaluation scores first,
-- by the תשע"ב evaluation (1)(ג) and (2)(ג) name. Ties at the last place
-- are all reached (convention thresholds.ties). A teacher is reached when
-- the positions of every teacher scored above him, with his own, fit in
-- the places left.
GIVEN `places` IS A NUMBER
      `score of` IS A FUNCTION FROM `candidate for the 1,800 positions` TO NUMBER
      cs IS A LIST OF `candidate for the 1,800 positions`
GIVETH A LIST OF `candidate for the 1,800 positions`
DECIDE `the candidates the places reach` `places` `score of` cs IS
    filter (GIVEN c YIELD
                sum (map `the positions a promotion takes from the 1,800`
                         (filter (GIVEN d YIELD `score of` d GREATER THAN `score of` c) cs))
                PLUS `the positions a promotion takes from the 1,800` c
                AT MOST `places`)
           cs

GIVEN c IS A `candidate for the 1,800 positions`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the תשע"ב score of` c IS c's `the תשע"ב evaluation score`

GIVEN c IS A `candidate for the 1,800 positions`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the תשע"ה score of` c IS c's `the תשע"ה evaluation score`

GIVEN cs IS A LIST OF `candidate for the 1,800 positions`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the positions taken by` cs IS
    sum (map `the positions a promotion takes from the 1,800` cs)

GIVEN c IS A `candidate for the 1,800 positions`, cs IS A LIST OF `candidate for the 1,800 positions`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the same teacher as one of` c cs IF
    any (GIVEN d YIELD d's `the candidate's number` EQUALS c's `the candidate's number`) cs

GIVEN cs IS A LIST OF `candidate for the 1,800 positions`
GIVETH A LIST OF `candidate for the 1,800 positions`
DECIDE `promoted in the first round` cs IS
    `the candidates the places reach` `the 1,800 positions` `the תשע"ב score of` (filter `meets the first round of §ח` cs)

GIVEN cs IS A LIST OF `candidate for the 1,800 positions`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `places left after the first round` cs IS
    `not below zero` (`the 1,800 positions` MINUS `the positions taken by` (`promoted in the first round` cs))

GIVEN cs IS A LIST OF `candidate for the 1,800 positions`
GIVETH A LIST OF `candidate for the 1,800 positions`
DECIDE `promoted in the second round` cs IS
    `the candidates the places reach` (`places left after the first round` cs) `the תשע"ב score of`
        (filter (GIVEN c YIELD `meets the second round of §ח` c AND NOT `is the same teacher as one of` c (`promoted in the first round` cs)) cs)

GIVEN cs IS A LIST OF `candidate for the 1,800 positions`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `places left after the second round` cs IS
    `not below zero` (`places left after the first round` cs MINUS `the positions taken by` (`promoted in the second round` cs))

GIVEN cs IS A LIST OF `candidate for the 1,800 positions`
GIVETH A LIST OF `candidate for the 1,800 positions`
DECIDE `promoted in the third round` cs IS
    `the candidates the places reach` (`places left after the second round` cs) `the תשע"ה score of`
        (filter (GIVEN c YIELD
                     `meets the third round's (א) and (ב)` c
                     AND NOT `is the same teacher as one of` c (`promoted in the first round` cs)
                     AND NOT `is the same teacher as one of` c (`promoted in the second round` cs))
                cs)

-- Worked examples: a full-position teacher in grade 6 seeking 7, who
-- finished the hours on 1.6.2014 and has 36 months in grade 6 by 1.9.2014.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, g IS A NUMBER, m14 IS A NUMBER, m15 IS A NUMBER, retires IS A BOOLEAN, s5775 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `candidate for the 1,800 positions`
DECIDE `a candidate` n g m14 m15 retires s5775 IS
    `candidate for the 1,800 positions` WITH
        `the candidate's number`  IS n
        `seeks grade`             IS g
        `position share`          IS 1
        `fills a grade-9 position free at the signing` IS FALSE
        `finished the professional-development hours on` IS JUST (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2014)
        `months counted in the grade below by 1.9.2014`  IS m14
        `months counted in the grade below by 1.8.2015`  IS m15
        `months counted in the grade below by 31.8.2015` IS m15
        `evaluated sufficient by the תשע"ב measures`     IS TRUE
        `the תשע"ב evaluation score`                      IS 80
        `retires on 31.8.2015`                            IS retires
        `the תשע"ה evaluation score`                      IS s5775

-- 36 months by 1.9.2014 meet the first round's §38(ו) (three years then);
-- 36 months by 1.8.2015 do not meet the second's (three years and a month).
#ASSERT `meets the first round of §ח` (`a candidate` 1 7 36 47 FALSE 0)
#ASSERT NOT `meets the second round of §ח` (`a candidate` 2 7 24 36 TRUE 0)
#ASSERT `meets the second round of §ח` (`a candidate` 3 9 26 37 TRUE 0)

-- Three for the third round, two places: the highest תשע"ה scores; at a tie
-- for the last place both are reached.
`three for the third round` MEANS LIST `a candidate` 4 7 10 37 FALSE 90, `a candidate` 5 8 10 37 FALSE 85, `a candidate` 6 7 10 37 FALSE 70
#ASSERT map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `the candidate's number`) (`the candidates the places reach` 2 `the תשע"ה score of` `three for the third round`) EQUALS LIST 4, 5
`two tied for one place` MEANS LIST `a candidate` 7 7 10 37 FALSE 85, `a candidate` 8 7 10 37 FALSE 85
#ASSERT count (`the candidates the places reach` 1 `the תשע"ה score of` `two tied for one place`) EQUALS 2

-- The rounds in turn: the first takes its own; the third ranks what is left.
`the rounds' candidates` MEANS LIST `a candidate` 1 7 36 47 FALSE 0, `a candidate` 4 7 10 37 FALSE 90, `a candidate` 5 8 10 37 FALSE 85
#ASSERT map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `the candidate's number`) (`promoted in the first round` `the rounds' candidates`) EQUALS LIST 1
#ASSERT `places left after the first round` `the rounds' candidates` EQUALS 1799
#ASSERT map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `the candidate's number`) (`promoted in the third round` `the rounds' candidates`) EQUALS LIST 4, 5
-- A grade-9 promotion into a position free at the signing takes nothing.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, share IS A NUMBER, s5772 IS A NUMBER, `free grade-9 position` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `candidate for the 1,800 positions`
DECIDE `a first-round candidate` n share s5772 `free grade-9 position` IS
    `candidate for the 1,800 positions` WITH
        `the candidate's number`  IS n
        `seeks grade`             IS 9
        `position share`          IS share
        `fills a grade-9 position free at the signing` IS `free grade-9 position`
        `finished the professional-development hours on` IS JUST (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2014)
        `months counted in the grade below by 1.9.2014`  IS 36
        `months counted in the grade below by 1.8.2015`  IS 47
        `months counted in the grade below by 31.8.2015` IS 47
        `evaluated sufficient by the תשע"ב measures`     IS TRUE
        `the תשע"ב evaluation score`                      IS s5772
        `retires on 31.8.2015`                            IS FALSE
        `the תשע"ה evaluation score`                      IS 0

#ASSERT `the positions a promotion takes from the 1,800` (`a first-round candidate` 9 1 80 TRUE) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the positions a promotion takes from the 1,800` (`a first-round candidate` 9 1 80 FALSE) EQUALS 1

-- F-ofek-hadash-2015-stay-periods-c's evidence: the first round, read as
-- printed, promotes every teacher who meets it, past 1,800 positions too —
-- here two groups of a thousand positions each (standing for as many
-- teachers); the order of §38(ח) reaches the higher-scored only.
`two thousand positions for the first round` MEANS LIST `a first-round candidate` 1 1000 90 FALSE, `a first-round candidate` 2 1000 80 FALSE

GIVEN cs IS A LIST OF `candidate for the 1,800 positions`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the positions the first round's words promote` cs IS
    `the positions taken by` (filter `meets the first round of §ח` cs)

`the rounds' words set no order where teachers outnumber the places` MEANS
        `the positions the first round's words promote` `two thousand positions for the first round` GREATER THAN `the 1,800 positions`
    AND map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `the candidate's number`) (`promoted in the first round` `two thousand positions for the first round`) EQUALS LIST 1
#ASSERT `the rounds' words set no order where teachers outnumber the places`

§§ `ט. מה אינו נגרע`

-- §§א–ו take nothing from §38(א), (ג), (ד), (ה), (ז), (ח), (י), (יא) and
-- §48 of the base agreement: those stand as imported (`base-agreement-38`).
@ref akn:art_i
`the subsections §ט keeps` MEANS LIST "38(א)", "38(ג)", "38(ד)", "38(ה)", "38(ז)", "38(ח)", "38(י)", "38(יא)", "48"

`§ט keeps the §38(ז) that §ו sets aside` MEANS
        elem "38(ז)" `the subsections §ט keeps`
    AND elem "38(ז)" `the subsections §ו sets aside`
    AND elem "38(ח)" `the subsections §ט keeps`
    AND elem "38(ח)" `the subsections §ג sets aside`
#ASSERT `§ט keeps the §38(ז) that §ו sets aside`

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:conclusions/p1 The signatures; no rule.
